SUMMARY:Your DC Moment | Dinner with Ambassador and Professor Lee Feinstein
DESCRIPTION:Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session for t
 he Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. Don't just study global leader
 ship. Put it into practice.  This intimate event is for students interest
 ed in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 residency. It's a working dinner and
  a peek at what a global career actually feels like before you step into 
 it.Why you should attend:Sit at the Table: Engage with leaders who have s
 haped global policy and international careers.    Alumni Insights: Hear f
 rom a panel of D.C. Program alumni regarding their on-the-ground experien
 ces.    Professional Roadmap: Get a technical walkthrough of the Spring 2
 027 cycle\, including the January 12 – May 2 residency dates.    The Lo
 gistics Bridge: Understand how the IU Capital Campus housing works and ho
 w the classes work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD students.    The Strat
 egy Session AgendaI. The Practitioner Perspective: A briefing from Ambass
 ador Lee Feinstein on D.C. professional realities and "tradecraft" skills
 .    II. The Roadmap: A deep dive into the October 15 deadline\, intervie
 w sprints (Oct 26–28)\, and the mandatory December 12 orientation.    I
 II. Housing &amp\; Classes: Guidance on the Capital Campus residency and 
 the academic courses offered in D.C.    IV. Ground Game: Peer-to-peer bre
 akouts and alumni panel discussion on commuting\, and professional life i
 n DC.    Biography: Ambassador &amp\; Professor Lee Feinstein  Ambassador
  Lee Feinstein is a Senior Managing Director and the President of McLarty
  Associates. He previously served as the U.S. Ambassador to the Republic 
 of Poland and held senior positions at the Department of State\, includin
 g Principal Deputy Director and a Member of the Policy Planning Staff. He
  was the Founding Dean of the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and Interna
 tional Studies at Indiana University from 2014 to 2022. Ambassador Feinst
 ein is a member of the Council on Foreign Relations and the American Acad
 emy of Diplomacy\, and holds a JD from Georgetown University Law Center. 
  &#160\;Can't make the full hour? No problem. This is a come-and-go strat
 egy session designed to fit your Thursday schedule.Link to Application:ht
 tps://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24a (https://iu.co1.qua
 ltrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW)
